These sample folders are for cobst/obmod/cprint.py exploration and development 
purposes.  

The Makefile & Makefile.inc combination works with the individual Makefiles 
to create debuggable executables from .cbl sources.  All the various 
intermediate files are left intact, as well as some files that aren't used for
anything.

The implicit warning is that this playground is not like a production 
environment.  Please don't try to turn it into one, and don't expect a 
production environment to produce results that look like what happens here.

Specifically, the current process is 
    cobc produces relocatable .o files and several listing files
    cobst reads the listing files and produces the .tab file
    obmod reads the .o file and modifies it into .cbl.o by modifying the .debug
            line table, and by embedding cprint.py
    cobc then converts .cbl.o into an executable.

In production, everything except the executable and .tab can be deleted.  The
executable and the .tab file must be co-located in the same directory in order
for cprint.py to work.

Bob Dubner 2019-08-13
